    {
      "id": "cutter",
      "steps": [
        {
          "record": "the cutter's PRB (mm)",
          "text": "Fit the cutter with its collar. Run tool-length calibration from the app’s console or Studio (M491).",
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not skip this because the program contains T1 M6. If the machine already believes tool 1 is fitted, that line does nothing.",
        },
      ],
      "title": "4 · Fit the cutter and measure its length",
    },
    {
      "id": "origin",
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "The vise already references X and rotation to within ±0.05 mm, before any touch.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Touch 1 of 3: the front edge — the one nearest you, about 25 mm along it from the left end — this gives position and rotation.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Touch 2 of 3: the front edge — the one nearest you, about 75 mm along it from the left end — this gives rotation.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Touch 3 of 3: the right edge — the one against the moving jaw, at about its middle, 30 mm from the front end — this gives X.",
        },
        {
          "record": "surface Z (mm) and the PRB of the tool that set Z0 (mm)",
          "text": "Z0: the blank's top face — probe it, or touch off on it. Record the reading AND the tool that made it: on a job cut by two cutters the second program’s Z0 is worked out from this surface and the PRB of whichever tool took this touch, so both go on this one blank — the first cutter’s own PRB is a separate reading, taken where it is fitted.",
        },
        {
          "text": "X0 Y0 Z0 is the top-front-left corner of the blank. That leaves the work origin within ±0.02 mm in X and Y and ±0.02° in rotation. Move there and check by eye before going on. How well YOU set it is not modelled: the file places the blank at this corner and judges the jaws against it, so an origin that is out by a little — or a blank sitting differently from what was measured — shifts the whole job relative to both without the app knowing. The only X/Y slack for that is this job's edge margin, 1 mm, which is the gap the content keeps from a stock edge rather than a locating tolerance: a cut standing at that margin has used all of it.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Rotation is measured, and a static .nc cannot compensate it (Smoothieware has no variables, §7.3 / #187 item 1): apply it in Studio's dialogs, or re-post with the rotation baked into the geometry",
        },
        {
          "text": "Z is always probed on the engraved face (§7.2): no fixture can supply it",
        },
        {
          "record": "surface Z at each point (mm), and how each was taken (probe / touch-off)",
          "text": "The blank's top is measured at 5 points across the cut — its centre, then both extents on each axis — because a printed blank’s colour line is a plane and its dome is extra material above it: one touch at the centre cannot tell you the floor at the ends of a line. Take them in the order below and write each reading down.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Surface touch 1 of 5: the cut area's centre, X 50 Y 27.463 — take the top there and record the reading.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Surface touch 2 of 5: the cut area's left extent, X 23.309 Y 27.463 — take the top there and record the reading.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Surface touch 3 of 5: the cut area's right extent, X 76.691 Y 27.463 — take the top there and record the reading.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Surface touch 4 of 5: the cut area's front extent, X 50 Y 4.766 — take the top there and record the reading.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Surface touch 5 of 5: the cut area's back extent, X 50 Y 50.16 — take the top there and record the reading.",
        },
        {
          "text": "This blank states no colour split, so only the ceiling limits the floors: they must stay at most 11 mm below the top (the blank's underside, including its 1 mm margin). A surface spread wider than that band cannot keep every floor past the colour line and clear of the pocket at the same time.",
          "value": "band 11 mm",
        },
        {
          "record": "the touch Z0 was set from, and the readings it came from",
          "text": "Set Z0 from the LOWEST of these 5 readings, not from the registration touch above and not from the centre alone. Every programmed floor depth is measured from Z0, so at a higher touch the local floor is deeper by exactly its height above Z0: with Z0 at the lowest reading, the programmed depth is the SHALLOWEST floor and the programmed depth plus the spread is the deepest.",
          "value": "Z0 = the lowest surface touch",
        },
        {
          "bold": true,
          "text": "If the lowest and highest readings differ by more than 11 mm, do not cut. The app refuses that blank as: “this blank is bowed <spread> mm across the cut; the floors cannot stay past the colour line and clear of the pocket”.",
        },
      ],
      "title": "5 · Set the work origin",
    },
    {
      "id": "dry-run",
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Load Untitled-engrave-job-frame.nc and run it. The cutter traces the job's outline in the air, 20 mm above the work — no Z offset to set. Watch that the trace stays over the blank and clear of the jaws.",
          "value": "20 mm above the work",
        },
        {
          "text": "If the trace is not where the job should land, stop and change the job. Otherwise load Untitled-engrave-job.nc and cut.",
        },
      ],
      "title": "6 · Dry run",
    },
    {
      "id": "cut",
      "steps": [
        {
          "text": "Spindle, feed, plunge, passes and step-down. Vacuum on.",
          "value": "12000 RPM · 500 mm/min feed · 200 mm/min plunge · 2 × 0.5 mm passes · 0.45 mm step-over",
        },
        {
          "text": "Engrave "CASE"",
          "value": "2 mm deep",
        },
        {
          "text": "Engrave "MAKER"",
          "value": "1 mm deep",
        },
        {
          "text": "Engrave "first chips"",
          "value": "0.5 mm deep",
        },
        {
          "text": "Stay at the machine. Stop it if the sound changes, the blank moves, or the cutter loads up.",
        },
      ],
      "title": "7 · Cut",
    },
    {
      "id": "warnings",
      "steps": [
        {
          "bold": true,
          "text": "Vise dimensions are the shipped defaults, measured once on the reference unit (#208); they are not a measurement of this machine's own vise.",
        },
        {
          "text": "Checked: the tool against the stock and the modelled fixture (Vise fixed jaw (left), Vise moving jaw (right)).",
        },
        {
          "text": "Not checked: the spindle body, head and gantry; anything on the bed other than the declared stock, workholding and sacrificial material.",
        },
        {
          "text": "The modelled fixture is a shipped default, not a measurement.",
        },
      ],
      "title": "8 · Warnings carried from the app",
    },
    {
      "id": "record",
      "steps": [
        {
          "record": "measured depth (mm)",
          "text": "Measured floor depth — Engrave "CASE"",
        },
        {
          "record": "measured depth (mm)",
          "text": "Measured floor depth — Engrave "MAKER"",
        },
        {
          "record": "measured depth (mm)",
          "text": "Measured floor depth — Engrave "first chips"",
        },
        {
          "record": "yes / no",
          "text": "Is the text legible?",
        },
        {
          "record": "clean / fuzzy / burnt",
          "text": "Surface finish",
        },
        {
          "record": "notes",
          "text": "Anything that went wrong",
        },
      ],
      "title": "9 · Record afterwards",
    },
  ],
  "toolProfileLegend": "DS shank diameter · DC cutting diameter · LC flute length · LS shoulder length",
  "toolProfileSvg": "<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="-73.19 -156.5 110.9 223.47" class="cutter-profile-svg cutter-profile--print" role="img" aria-label="1 mm flat end (assumed) — flat end mill profile" style="color:#111111;--cutter-missing:#8a1c1c;--cutter-muted:#555555"><title>1 mm flat end (assumed) — flat end mill profile</title><desc>Side profile of 1 mm flat end (assumed), drawn from its Tool record: a flat end mill. Stated: DS 3.175 (shank diameter), DC 1.0 (cutting diameter). Not stated, drawn dashed: LS shoulder length, LC flute length.</desc><path d="M0,0 L5.14,0 L5.14,-41.14 L5.14,-66.86 L16.33,-66.86 L16.33,-148.5 L-16.33,-148.5 L-16.33,-148.5 L-16.33,-66.86 L-5.14,-66.86 L-5.14,-41.14 L-5.14,0 L0,0 Z" fill="#f4f4f4" stroke="none" fill-opacity="1" /><path d="M0,0 L5.14,0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M0,0 L-5.14,0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M5.14,0 L5.14,-41.14" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-5.14,0 L-5.14,-41.14" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M5.14,-41.14 L5.14,-66.86" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-5.14,-41.14 L-5.14,-66.86" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M5.14,-66.86 L16.33,-66.86" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-5.14,-66.86 L-16.33,-66.86" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M16.33,-66.86 L16.33,-148.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-16.33,-66.86 L-16.33,-148.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-16.33,-148.5 L-8.16,-143.5 L0,-148.5 L8.16,-143.5 L16.33,-148.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M0,20.57 L0,-148.5" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-muted, currentColor)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-dasharray="4 3" opacity="0.45" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-5.14,0 L5.14,0" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-muted, currentColor)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-dasharray="4 3" opacity="0.45" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><g class="cutter-profile__dimension" data-dimension="DS" data-field="handleDiameter"><path d="M-16.33,-107.68 L16.33,-107.68" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-16.33,-107.68 L-12.33,-105.88 L-12.33,-109.48 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" /><path d="M16.33,-107.68 L12.33,-109.48 L12.33,-105.88 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" /><path d="M-16.33,-66.86 L-16.33,-107.68" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-muted, currentColor)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M16.33,-66.86 L16.33,-107.68" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-muted, currentColor)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><rect x="-21.72" y="-120.18" width="43.44" height="10.5" fill="#f4f4f4" /><text x="0" y="-111.68" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="8.5" font-weight="400" fill="#111111">DS 3.175</text></g><g class="cutter-profile__dimension" data-dimension="DC" data-field="tipDiameter"><path d="M-5.14,-18.51 L5.14,-18.51" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-5.14,-18.51 L-1.14,-16.71 L-1.14,-20.31 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" /><path d="M5.14,-18.51 L1.14,-20.31 L1.14,-16.71 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" /><rect x="-16.79" y="-31.01" width="33.58" height="10.5" fill="#f4f4f4" /><text x="0" y="-22.51" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="8.5" font-weight="400" fill="#111111">DC 1.0</text></g><g class="cutter-profile__dimension is-missing" data-dimension="LS" data-field="shoulderLength"><path d="M-30.33,-66.86 L-30.33,0" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="0.7" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-30.33,-66.86 L-32.13,-62.86 L-28.53,-62.86 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" /><path d="M-30.33,0 L-28.53,-4 L-32.13,-4 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" /><path d="M-16.33,-66.86 L-30.33,-66.86" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-5.14,0 L-30.33,0" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><text x="-35.33" y="-30.43" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="8.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" transform="rotate(-90 -35.33 -30.43)">LS ?</text></g><g class="cutter-profile__dimension is-missing" data-dimension="LC" data-field="fluteLength"><path d="M-50.33,-41.14 L-50.33,0" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="0.7" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-50.33,-41.14 L-52.13,-37.14 L-48.53,-37.14 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" /><path d="M-50.33,0 L-48.53,-4 L-52.13,-4 Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none" /><path d="M-5.14,-41.14 L-50.33,-41.14" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><path d="M-5.14,0 L-50.33,0" fill="none" stroke="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" stroke-width="0.6" stroke-dasharray="4 3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><text x="-55.33" y="-17.57" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="8.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--cutter-missing, #8a1c1c)" transform="rotate(-90 -55.33 -17.57)">LC ?</text></g><g class="cutter-profile__scale"><path d="M-25.71,42.57 L25.71,42.57" fill="none" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="1" /><path d="M-25.71,38.57 L-25.71,46.57" fill="none" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="1" /><path d="M25.71,38.57 L25.71,46.57" fill="none" stroke="#111111" stroke-width="1" /><text x="0" y="55.57" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="8" font-weight="400" fill="#111111">scale 5 mm</text></g></svg>",
}
